  "result": "Perfect! All 110 tests pass. Here's what I implemented for VAT:\n\n\u2705 **Added `lineVat(line)` function**\n- Calculates VAT on the line's amount **after discount**\n- Formula: (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate \u00f7 100\n- Result clamped at 0 and rounded with `roundCents()`\n\n\u2705 **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- **subtotal**: sum of all line totals (pre-discount)\n- **discount**: sum of all line discounts\n- **vat**: sum of all rounded line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n- **total**: subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n\u2705 **Key decision: VAT per line**\n- Each line's VAT is calculated and rounded independently\n- Invoice VAT is the sum of these rounded values\n- This prevents rounding errors that would occur with a single invoice-level percentage\n\n\u2705 **Updated `renderInvoiceText`** to display VAT\n- Shows \"VAT: \u20ac...\" on its own line when vat > 0\n- Positioned just above the total\n- All amounts formatted through `formatEuros()`\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests** (23 new) covering:\n- `lineVat` with various discount and VAT rate combinations\n- `invoiceTotals` with VAT calculations\n- Mixed VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- VAT with discounts\n- VAT-exempt items\n- Render output with VAT",
